#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""berth — occupancy of a file identity.

Ancestor roost/perch splits a still-TRUE run when the witness set changes,
but exists of an exact path cannot: the holder *is* the path, so a rename is
a death plus a birth. berth --follow treats the rename as one identity.
Occupancy stays TRUE; holders still split (old path → new path).

--no-follow recovers path occupancy. --boolean recovers ancestor held.
"""

